  "id": "priming",
  "term": "priming",
  "definition": "Priming is an effect in which earlier exposure to related meaning, such as a shared morpheme or word element, changes how quickly or accurately a later item is processed. In language tasks it often helps access meaning, but under some conditions it can instead interfere and produce inhibition.",
